n finance reform so the more not  millionaires do not continue to buy  seats in the United States Congress what  the Progressive Caucus promises the  American people today is that we will do  all that we can in committees on the  floor of the house and in our  communities to expose the contract with  america for what it is and then to fight  for sensible alternatives ultimately the  final decision will be made by the  american people if you are concerned  about the contract with america and its  implications for the most vulnerable  people in our society then tell it to  the President and tell it to the members  that represent you ah thank you let me  now introduce major Owens a congressman  from New York City I think this caucus  has made it clear that the programs to  create jobs are our number one concern  and every step and this 104th Congress  we're going to move in ways to emphasize  the fact that we care about jobs we've  heard the voice of the majority of  Americans they made it quite clear and  the exit polls on Election Day in  numerous studies and the polls that  people are concerned about their jobs  those who have jobs of great anxieties  about keeping those jobs other people  feel they're underpaid and there's a  vast number of people we know who are  unemployed so at every step in the way  including this first 100 days we are  going to take steps to emphasize the  fact that the voice of the American  people are not being voices are not  being heard on the issue of jobs on the  balanced budget amendment for example we  intend to offer an amendment which we  call our fiscal Fairness Act which  merely states that employment job  creation investment in jobs as we  propose at our investment jobs at  investment of jobs are equal to national  security equal to threats to national  security at war they have a provision  which says Congress may waive the  provisions of this article meaning the  provisions of  balanced budget amendment for any fiscal  year and 